{"nodes": [{"id": "roadmap_v0_16_0", "label": "v0.16.0 release", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "The entry points, logging and old defects release - 181 commits, the largest window so far.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_subsystem_entry_points", "label": "Core-only root export with per-subsystem entries (#414)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "One barrel shipped the testkit in the production entry and made importing ActorSystem pay for whatever any subsystem pulled in eagerly; eighteen subsystems now get their own entry and the smoke suite loads every declared entry on all three runtimes.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_logging_sink_architecture", "label": "Logging sink architecture (#1150)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The logger wrote to exactly one place; it now fans one record out to console, rotating files and ten log platforms, each dependency-free, with nothing about the existing surface changed.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_bug_security_wave", "label": "50-oldest bug and security wave", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "42 of the 50 oldest open defects resolved, batched by which files they touch rather than by module label; independent verification found five regressions the wave itself introduced, each repaired with the failing test written first.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_gossip_sequence_field", "label": "GossipMessage required sequence field (#112)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "BREAKING: an upgraded peer refuses an old node's frames and an old node ignores the new field, so a rolling upgrade does not converge in either direction; the guard also holds only while the sender is still a member, which needs #940's incarnation identity to close.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_production_goal_wave", "label": "50-oldest production-goal wave", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Triage before code was the expensive half: 277 claims in the issue bodies did not survive an independent pass asking whether the acceptance criteria were met rather than whether the defect still existed.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_typecheck_dev", "label": "typecheck:dev gate (#540)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "From 320 errors to green and gated; the burn-down was not the point - it was hiding five exported declarations no caller could use, each compiling for the library and breaking only at a call site.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_unreachability_not_reconciled", "label": "Unreachability deliberately not reconciled", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "On the no-lease path 'hosted somewhere' and 'at most one' cannot both hold, because reaching the incumbent to ask it to stand down is what failed; a quorum gate was designed and rejected as a split-brain resolver at a layer with no downing state.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_v0_15_0", "label": "v0.15.0 - mailboxes and channels", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_unbounded_mailbox_default", "label": "Unbounded mailbox is the default again (#1148)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "BREAKING: a mailbox cannot tell a stale sample from a control message, so drop-head on every actor was never confined to the telemetry-shaped workloads it suits; ActorCell now warns at 10 000 queued messages and every doubling after.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_drop_reporting_mailbox", "label": "DropReportingMailbox (#1149, #661)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The cell registers its drop observer after choosing the mailbox, so a mailbox supplied through withMailbox is no longer invisible to actor_mailbox_dropped_total.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_event_key", "label": "EventKey event-stream channels (#1143)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Channels can be kind-discriminated types via a new EventKey mirroring ServiceKey and ShardKey; publishing something nobody could subscribe to was possible before this.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_constants_placement_rule", "label": "Constants placement rule (#1142)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Four possible homes checked in order, written down in AGENTS.md; ~300 constants across 130 files audited against it with every public name unchanged.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_v0_13_0", "label": "v0.13.0 - names and lifecycle", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_props_removed", "label": "Props removed (#547)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "spawn(MyActor, name); per-actor configuration is ActorOptions, a regular XOptions family - the one place in the framework that did not follow that convention.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_sharding_lifecycle", "label": "Sharding passivation lifecycle (#892)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Idle entities passivate after five minutes by default and empty shards stop with them, via shardPassivationIdleMs.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_devtools_suite", "label": "DevTools suite (#445)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Seven panels on one versioned tap protocol behind a ./devtools export; absorbed the separately listed live cluster visualizer (#204).", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_documentation_site", "label": "Documentation site (#26)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_audit_round_1166_1193", "label": "Audit round #1166-#1193 (unstarted)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Holds several priority: high correctness defects - PersistentActor has no fencing (#1166), throttle('pause') livelocks the MicrotaskDispatcher (#1167), KeepMajority leaves both sides running on an exact tie (#1170), and ShardCoordinator ignores the configured shard count (#1026).", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "roadmap_out_of_scope", "label": "Explicitly out of scope", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Auto-magic cache invalidation by tag or pattern is a known bug-source, so invalidation stays explicit via cache.delete(...); no backwards-compatibility guarantees pre-1.0; pull requests are not accepted, well-shaped issues are.", "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "roadmap_v0_16_0", "target": "readme_actor_ts", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_v0_16_0", "target": "roadmap_subsystem_entry_points", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_v0_16_0", "target": "roadmap_logging_sink_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_v0_16_0", "target": "roadmap_bug_security_wave", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_bug_security_wave", "target": "roadmap_gossip_sequence_field", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_production_goal_wave", "target": "roadmap_typecheck_dev", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_production_goal_wave", "target": "roadmap_unreachability_not_reconciled", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "ROADMAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "roadmap_v0_15_0", "target": "r